function.arguments:
{"description": "Model the Capacitated Vehicle Routing Problem with Hard Time Windows (VRPHTW) in MILP form.

Data: one depot (node 0) and customers 1..n (e.g., Solomon instance r101 with n=100 customers). Each customer i has demand q_i, service duration s_i, and hard time window [e_i, l_i] (service must start within the window; early arrival means waiting). Depot has time window [e_0, l_0]. A fleet of K identical vehicles with capacity Q is available at the depot. Travel time and cost between nodes i,j is t_ij (assume t_ij = Euclidean distance, symmetric, t_ii = 0; travel cost = travel time). Vehicles depart from and return to the depot; each vehicle performs at most one route. Each customer must be served by exactly one vehicle. Capacity constraints must hold on every route. Delays beyond l_i are not allowed (hard windows); waiting before e_i is allowed at no cost. Objective: minimize total travel cost (total distance traveled).

Provide: decision variables (binary arc variables x_ij for vehicle usage of arc (i,j), continuous arrival/service-start time variables T_i, and load variables L_i or similar for subtour/capacity elimination), full objective, all constraints (degree constraints, fleet size, capacity via load propagation, time-window feasibility via big-M time propagation, subtour elimination via time/load variables), and state all assumptions explicitly (homogeneous fleet, single depot, service starts within window, waiting allowed, K can be fixed or upper-bounded by n)."}

